    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nExternal routers can attach SGLang PD routing metadata to OpenAI-compatible requests, but the Anthropic `/v1/messages` path currently drops that metadata when converting `AnthropicMessagesRequest` to `ChatCompletionRequest`. This prevents Anthropic-compatible requests from carrying fields such as `bootstrap_room` into the existing PD disaggregation flow.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Add the five existing PD routing fields to `AnthropicMessagesRequest`.\r\n- Forward them unchanged when constructing `ChatCompletionRequest`.\r\n- Add a regression test covering all five fields.\r\n\r\nThis is limited to the Anthropic request conversion boundary. It does not modify OpenAI endpoints, response formats, or PD core logic.\r\n\r\nLocal checks:\r\n- `scripts/ci/check_registered_tests.py`\r\n- Python bytecode compilation for all changed files\r\n- Field declaration/forwarding structural checks\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n\r\nThe focused runtime unit test is included and will run in CI; the local macOS checkout does not have the full SGLang runtime dependency set installed.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNot applicable. This change only forwards request routing metadata and does not affect model computation or outputs.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot applicable. This change adds direct request-field forwarding only.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (Not required: no public protocol surface is introduced.)\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (Not applicable; see above.)\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #30782572239](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30782572239)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #30782572096](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30782572096)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
